ar. Expert raters disagree: Cook, Fox News and the Economist call it a Tossup, several outlets lean Republican for a flip, and two lean Democratic. The limited polling available, all from Democratic-leaning sponsors, shows a race within a couple of points either way. Prediction markets price the Democrat at roughly even odds. With no incumbent and a volatile recent partisan history, this is one of the most competitive House races in Florida.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.5161, "margin": 0.22}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.4293, "margin": -1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.5493, "margin": 0.2}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.5402, "margin": 0.2}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.4658, "margin": 0.0}]}